Sailworks is a fork of GWeatherRouting
(https://github.com/dakk/gweatherrouting), originally written by Davide Gessa
and contributors. The fork point is commit a750e4d on the `dev` branch. The
complete record of changes since that commit is the project's git history.

Since the fork point this project has been renamed from GWeatherRouting to
Sailworks (Python package, distribution name, command line entry points and
desktop files), its Qt front end and rendering pipeline have been largely
rewritten, and its weather data handling, packaging and documentation have been
modified. Files carried over from upstream keep their original copyright
notices.

The GPL grants rights in the software only. It does not grant rights to the
GWeatherRouting name or logo (see GPLv3 section 7(e)), which remain with the
upstream project. "Sailworks" and this project's own branding are separate from
upstream.

Bundled third-party components and assets, with their licenses and origins, are
recorded in sailworks/data/COPYRIGHT.

